  "content": {
    "title": "How to stream March Madness games for free: Streaming services to watch NCAA Tournament",
    "text": "March 17, 2026, 3:06 p.m. ETThe Men's NCAA Tournament kicks off in just a few hours in Dayton with the First Four.It signals the start of one of the all-time great postseason tournaments, where legends are made and Cinderellas can be created at any time. And though the First Four takes place at night and after working hours, part of the charm of March Madness is that it gives avid and casual college basketball fans a plethora of games to watch throughout the entire day over the first two weekends.This is especially true when the first round begins on Thursday with games running from just past noon ET until late into the night from coast to coast. It's part of the chaos that often breaks out during the single-elimination tournament, and what makes it one of the best weeks on the sports calendar.Stream select NCAA Tournament games with Fubo (free trial)So, the question now becomes: have you finalized your TV schedule for Thursday and Friday's slate of first-round games? How will you watch all the games? Which games will you want to watch on the Quad Box, and which games will be left off until there is an in-studio highlight check-in during a different game's broadcast that makes you flip to that new game?Those are all loaded questions, and rightfully so, as everyone wants to watch upsets take place and potential buzzer-beaters. But don't worry, there are ways to ease the stress and watch those games that don't fit on the television, so that you get to experience and take in as much of the madness as you can in a single day.Here's what to know about how to stream Men's NCAA Tournament games over the next few weeks:How to stream March Madness games for freeFree March Madness streaming options: March Madness Live app | Fubo (free trial)There are two free streaming options for the Men's NCAA Tournament, aside from watching games that air nationally on CBS, which is a linear TV channel offering.The first option is Fubo, which carries CBS and offers a free trial to new subscribers. CBS will televise 21 games of this year's tournament.The other option is the March Madness Live app. Those who have CBS or one of the Turner Sports Networks channels — TBS, TNT and truTV — as part of their TV packages, they can sign into the March Madness Live app with their TV login credentials and watch off their phones or tablets. The same will work for watching games on a laptop through the March Madness Live webpage on the NCAA website.March Madness streaming options: How to livestream NCAA Tournament gamesStreaming options: March Madness Live app | Sling TV | Fubo (free trial)In addition to the March Madness Live app and Fubo, Sling TV is another streaming option for March Madness games. Sling TV is a streaming option for games that will appear on TBS, TNT and truTV.TBS will each televise 21 games, while truTV will air or simulcast a total of 24 games throughout the tournament, and TNT will air or simulcast a total of 15 games. The Final Four and national championship will also air on TBS, meaning Sling TV and the March Madness Live app are the only streaming options for those two rounds of the Men's NCAA Tournament.",
